te who wants more out of his life than making honey, decides to sue the human race after learning about the exploitation of bees at the hands of mankind. What will happen next?","popularity":11.3146,"poster_path":"/tX2mgKFUkzFMZingSVD4vioZNz2.jpg","release_date":"2007-10-28","softcore":false,"video":false,"vote_average":6.051,"vote_count":5489},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/jtOvTVlkF8TlaOq94oNXRc9u2yp.jpg","genre_ids":[12,16,10751,14],"id":5255,"title":"The Polar Express","original_language":"en","original_title":"The Polar Express","overview":"When a doubting young boy takes an extraordinary train ride to the North Pole, he embarks on a journey of self-discovery that shows him that the wonder of life never fades for those who believe.","popularity":12.6595,"poster_path":"/eOoCzH0MqeGr2taUZO4SwG416PF.jpg","release_date":"2004-11-10","softcore":false,"video":false,"vote_average":6.729,"vote_count":7125},{"adult":false,"backdrop_path":"/zBW4LZyYi0Moqz82BTkEQzR7h0z.jpg","genre_ids":[12,16,35,10751,14],"id":5393,"title":"Happily N'Ever After","original_language":"en","original_title":"Happily N'Ever After","overview":"An alliance of evil-doers, led by Frieda, looks to take over Fairy Tale Land. But when Ella realizes her stepmother is out to ruin her storybook existence, she takes a dramatic turn and blossoms into the leader of the resistance effort.","popularity":3.2753,"poster_path":"/geXsapJfihg78gVDvEVPoK5c07y.jpg","release_date":"2007-01-05","softcore":false,"video":false,"vote_average":5.1,"vote_count":458}],"total_pages":1001,"total_results":20001},"release_dates":{"results":[{"iso_3166_1":"GB","release_dates":[{"certification":"","descriptors":[],"iso_639_1":"","note":"BFI London Film Festival","release_date":"2026-10-11T00:00:00.000Z","type":1},{"certification":"12A","descriptors":[],"iso_639_1":"","note":"","release_date":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z","type":3}]},{"iso_3166_1":"US","release_dates":[{"certification":"PG-13","descriptors":[],"iso_639_1":"","note":"","release_date":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z","type":3},{"certification":"PG-13","descriptors":[],"iso_639_1":"","note":"","release_date":"2026-12-08T00:00:00.000Z","type":4}]}]},"keywords":{"keywords":[{"id":818,"name":"based on novel or book"},{"id":1896,"name":"portland, oregon"},{"id":2673,"name":"horse"},{"id":11107,"name":"rescue mission"},{"id":5774,"name":"forest"},{"id":1897,"name":"oregon, usa"},{"id":10121,"name":"stop motion"},{"id":193517,"name":"coyote"},{"id":272301,"name":"owl"},{"id":278823,"name":"3d animation"},{"id":294629,"name":"enchanted forest"},{"id":329731,"name":"fairytale"}]},"external_ids":{"imdb_id":"tt2056785","wikidata_id":"Q123058740","facebook_id":null,"instagram_id":null,"twitter_id":null},"watch/providers":{"results":{"US":{"link":"https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/791523-wildwood/watch?locale=US","buy":[{"logo_path":"/wpOt6x0dRxTrIzuBosto4LGd7E9.png","provider_id":7,"provider_name":"Fandango At Home","display_priority":40}]}}},"alternative_titles":{"titles":[{"iso_3166_1":"UA","title":"Дикий ліс","type":""},{"iso_3166_1":"RU","title":"Дикий лес","type":""},{"iso_3166_1":"TR","title":"Vahşi Orman","type":""},{"iso_3166_1":"MX","title":"El Bosque Salvaje: Wildwood","type":""},{"iso_3166_1":"CZ","title":"Wildwood: Tajemství zakázaného lesa","type":""},{"iso_3166_1":"FR","title":"Wildwood : La prophétie de la forêt","type":""},{"iso_3166_1":"AR","title":"Wildwood: El Bosque Salvaje","type":""},{"iso_3166_1":"HU","title":"Wildwood - A tiltott vadon","type":""}]},"reviews":{"page":1,"results":[{"author":"Manuel São Bento","author_details":{"name":"Manuel São Bento","username":"msbreviews","avatar_path":null,"rating":10},"content":"Check out my full review @ https://www.manuelsbento.com/wildwood-2026-laika-delivers-a-stop-motion-generational-masterpiece/\r\n\r\nRating: A+\r\n\r\nWILDWOOD is a true masterpiece, and I don't use that word lightly. Travis Knight and everyone at Laika spent years building, by hand, the most impressive stop-motion movie I've ever seen, one that deserves the \"generational classic\" stamp. Caleb Deschanel's cinematography and Dario Marianelli's score belong in every major awards conversation, as the final battle sits right next to the greatest set pieces ever put to screen. Peyton Elizabeth Lee and Jacob Tremblay carry two beautiful arcs. Carey Mulligan makes sorrow terrifying and heartbreaking at the same time. It's a dark, brave, deeply emotional story about grief, family, sacrifice, and, in a very Tolkien manner, the courage of small creatures and their everyday deeds to keep darkness at bay. No notes. I'll forever cherish this treasure.","created_at":"2026-10-23T15:10:06Z","id":"6adb78ce5c0b39dee051a6c9","updated_at":"2026-10-23T15:10:06Z","url":"https://www.themoviedb.org/review/6adb78ce5c0b39dee051a6c9"},{"author":"nkuk","author_details":{"name":"","username":"nkuk","avatar_path":null,"rating":5},"content":"Technically its a marvel, but storywise it really falls flat. \r\n\r\nThe stop-motion animation is so well done and fluid it looks like it could be computer generated. It must have taken an absolutely mammoth effort to create the film. The film has a painterly palette which looks gorgeous. Which is all the more shame as the characters and story let it down.\r\n\r\nThe characters are less than one dimensional. The parents make some of the most bizarre and illogical actions ever set to screen. Prue doesn't believe in magic she says, but never ever questions it. The other characters are under-developed cliches. The core of the story has conflicting messages and just washed over me, I didn't develop any affinity for any of the characters or end up rooting for them, and the film didn't connect with me on any level emotionally.\r\n\r\nThe film looks gorgeous, but there is nothing under the surface.","created_at":"2026-10-23T20:20:04Z","id":"6adbc174fdec4c9f8ea3e92c","updated_at":"2026-10-24T01:13:03Z","url":"https://www.themoviedb.org/review/6adbc174fdec4c9f8ea3e92c"},{"author":"andrewtislercinephile","author_details":{"name":"","username":"andrewtislercinephile","avatar_path":"/5MAF7xuZzVNgjrj8Sxns4D7H5oL.png","rating":8},"content":"Laika has always been one of my least favorite animation studios, and it's because they are tied to a medium of animation (stop-motion) that is becoming more and more dated as CGI is trying to replicate it with new software, and *Wildwood* is no exception. This movie is based on a 2011 novel about a teenager named Prue McKeel, who ventures into a forbidden forest to retrieve her baby brother Mac from the dowager governess, Alexandra. While the movie itself has a great story that perfectly blends action, comedy, character development, solid pacing, and emotional moments, and even has a phenomenal score from Dario Marianelli, the film's edgy, PG-13-level tone and stop motion visuals, while alluring, feel like a major letdown. The character designs look so stiff and plastic, almost like moving dolls rather than real people. And that's my problem with stop motion animation: the texture doesn't feel human and is not even trying to hide the materials it uses. The hair doesn't look like real human hair follicles, and the skin looks like it was made from silicone or clay (which it was). I am honestly not upset this movie is flopping at the box office, as stop motion animation has always been both a tricky medium to work with and a time-consuming one that takes too much out of an animators' day. It's very well-written and even the voice actors make up for some of the creepy character designs, not to mention that final scene of Prue stopping Alexandra is one of the most inspiring scenes in all of animated fiction, the uncanny visuals and slightly dark tone do drag it down. We have to","created_at":"2026-10-28T15:42:09Z","id":"6ae217d11392108dae048603","updated_at":"2026-10-28T15:42:09Z","url":"https://www.themoviedb.org/review/6ae217d11392108dae048603"}],"total_pages":1,"total_results":4}}
